        /// <term><b>Summary:</b></term>
        /// <summary>
        /// <para>Prepares the SCIM receiving configuration and returns the provisioning URL and credential summary. Issues a token if no available credentials exist and returns the plaintext only in the current response without automatically enabling user synchronization in AgentCore.</para>
        /// </summary>
        /// 
        /// <term><b>Description:</b></term>
        /// <description>
        /// <para>Prepares the receiving endpoint and access token for integrating SCIM user synchronization with an enterprise identity system. The enterprise identity system uses this information to provision users to the shared user pool of AgentCore.
        /// SCIM is a user provisioning protocol. The enterprise identity system first sends users to the receiving endpoint, and then AgentCore synchronizes the users from the user pool to the workspace.</para>
        /// <h3>Before you begin</h3>
        /// <para>A <c>CustomSSO</c> binding has been created by calling <a href="https://api.aliyun.com/document/AgentCore/2026-08-04/CreateIdentityProvider">CreateIdentityProvider</a>, and the shared user pool is ready. SCIM integration can be performed independently of SAML logon configuration.</para>
        /// <h3>What this operation prepares</h3>
        /// <para>This operation enables the SCIM receiving endpoint and returns the receiving URL and credential summary:</para>
        /// <table>
        /// <thead>
        /// <tr>
        /// <th>Current credential status</th>
        /// <th>Return result</th>
        /// </tr>
        /// </thead>
        /// <tbody><tr>
        /// <td>An unexpired credential with the status of <c>Enabled</c> already exists</td>
        /// <td>Reuses the existing credential. The <c>token</c> field returns an empty string <c>&quot;&quot;</c>. Use the previously saved token.</td>
        /// </tr>
        /// <tr>
        /// <td>No available credentials exist</td>
        /// <td>Creates a new credential. The <c>token</c> field returns the plaintext of the new token, which is returned only in the current response.</td>
        /// </tr>
        /// <tr>
        /// <td>The plaintext of an existing token cannot be queried again. If the token is lost, you can create a new token by calling <a href="https://api.aliyun.com/document/AgentCore/2026-08-04/CreateIdentityProviderSCIMCredential">CreateIdentityProviderSCIMCredential</a>. A single user pool can retain a maximum of two credentials. When the limit is reached, you must delete unused credentials first.</td>
        /// <td></td>
        /// </tr>
        /// </tbody></table>
